# width: 120
# A toast from the command that raised the one still on screen replaces
# it instead of stacking a second box (`App.toastLevel`; the source key
# is the command run): cycling the launcher dock twice reads one
# `dock: always` box where it used to read `dock: hidden` above
# `dock: always`. The proof is the stack's cap — five transient boxes,
# the oldest dropped for a sixth: `first word` goes up before the
# first cycle and four toasts follow it, so a second box for the dock
# would push `first word` off, and a replacement leaves it up.
# (A `lacks` on a toast proves nothing: the check polls, and the box
# it looks for expires on its own.)
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
ex echo first word
command view.dock_cycle_mode
expect screen contains "dock: hidden"
ex echo second word
ex echo third word
ex echo fourth word
command view.dock_cycle_mode
expect screen contains "dock: always"
expect screen contains "first word"
expect screen contains "second word"
expect screen contains "third word"
expect screen contains "fourth word"
